  "mechanism_narrative": "ERBB4-INSR forced-proximity novokine with exposit_rigid linker biases signaling toward MAPK/ERK and PI3K/AKT via transphosphorylation-recruited GRB2/SHC1/IRS1/FRS2/GAB1/PIK3R1/PTPN11 adaptors, while sterically excluding PLCG1/PLCG2 (Ca2+ branch) and SOS1/SOS2/RASA1 (direct RAS-GEF/RAS-GAP). The biased output upregulates muscle structural genes (ACTA2, MYL9, MYH11, MYOM2, TAGLN) and downregulates aged-marker IEGs (EGR1, FOS, JUN, TXNIP, IL32) and sarcomeric stress genes (TTN, NEB, MYH9), consistent with a rejuvenating transcriptome shift in aged skeletal muscle.",
